  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This serves 4 and takes about 35 minutes plus 1 hour marinating. The thing to watch is the heat: suya needs very high heat for short periods. If the heat is too low, the beef steams rather than chars and you lose the smoky, caramelised crust."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Slice the beef as thin as you can, about 5mm, across the grain. Thin slices cook fast and absorb the spice rub on both sides. Thick chunks are harder to grill evenly on a skewer."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
